pve-ext (0.2.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The page list is prefetched once at script load instead of fetched
    synchronously per config panel; a panel built before the answer arrives
    gets its tabs afterwards, and a failed request is not remembered as an
    empty list: the next config panel asks again.
  * The loader's header says why Ext.override cannot be used ('use strict'
    and callParent), instead of blaming ExtJS.
  * The loader no longer substitutes {vmid}, {node}, {type}, {theme} or
    {query} into a page's script URL, nor reads the theme cookie: no page
    uses them, and a page gets vmid, node and type as its config. It no
    longer re-checks a manifest's fields, which GET /ext/pages already
    does.
  * pve-ext-patch reads JSON manifests (<name>.json, a "files" array of the
    same fields) with core Perl's JSON::PP instead of a TOML subset in awk;
    pve-ext's own is pve-manager.json. Breaks pve-meta (<< 0.3.3~), whose
    older manifest is TOML. A manifest that does not parse stops the
    command before it touches a file.
  * pve-ext-patch: a failure is reported on stderr only, no longer also
    appended to /run/pve-ext-patch/failed and syslog.
  * pve-ext-patch: apply, verify and status rebuild pristine + diff with one
    helper; apply patches its scratch copy once instead of a dry run and
    then the same patch. verify counts a failed hunk once, no longer also
    by patch's summary line, and a scratch copy that cannot be made is
    said as such, not as a hunk count.
  * pve-ext-patch: cmd_status_quiet, which was cmd_status under another
    name, is gone; apply and remove call cmd_status.
  * debian/triggers also watches index.html.tpl.pve-ext-orig and
    API2.pm.pve-ext-orig, the names dpkg writes a pve-manager upgrade to
    while the files are diverted: the patch is re-applied on the new files
    again, instead of the old patched copies staying live until a manual
    pve-ext-patch apply. README ("Managed patches") asks the same of a
    package using pve-ext-patch.

 -- Julius Arkenberg <julius@rkenberg.de>  Fri, 25 Sep 2026 03:32:34 +0200

pve-ext (0.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The manifest id, the .claimed-by marker, the manifest-id subcommand and
    the no-stacking refusal are gone; a file another package has diverted is
    still refused. A leftover marker is ignored. Tabs are no longer gated on
    capabilities, and the iframe page form is gone: every page is a script
    with an xtype. A page manifest is checked for the fields the loader needs
    and skipped with a warning otherwise.

 -- Julius Arkenberg <julius@rkenberg.de>  Mon, 21 Sep 2026 17:09:00 +0200

pve-ext (0.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: PVE::API2::Ext (API-module discovery), pve-ext-loader.js
    (UI-page discovery) and pve-ext-patch (generic managed-patch tool),
    plus pve-ext's own two-file pve-manager patch manifest.

 -- Julius Arkenberg <julius@rkenberg.de>  Mon, 07 Sep 2026 12:00:00 -0000
